<li class="relative pl-5 before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-0 before:text-current [ul_&amp;]:before:content-[&#x27;•&#x27;] [ol_&amp;]:[counter-increment:item] [ol_&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)&#x27;)&#x27;] flex flex-col gap-y-(--spacing-sm)"><p class="wrapped">Strings that are not fully whitespace(e.g. <code class="[word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] inline-block font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-200))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs)">px-4</code>, <code class="[word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] inline-block font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-200))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs)">flex</code>, etc.). If there&#x27;s <span class="italic me-1">some</span> whitespace it&#x27;s not a problem and it will be trimmed without any warnings.</p></li>
